"01_dll_handle.mst — the `handle` instance variable `DynamicLinkLibrary`
 should have, supplied where `ResourceLibrary` can inherit it.

 `genprims` generates a `DynamicLinkLibrary` that is little more than a name:
 a `default` answering the class (so `Xxx default foo` and `Xxx foo` reach the
 same generated methods) plus one FFI entry point. Dolphin's real class is the
 base of the external-library machinery and carries `handle`, `basicOpen:`,
 `close`, `free` and the rest.

 `External.ResourceLibrary` is translated from the corpus and SUBCLASSES it,
 and its own code reads the inherited variable directly:

     (self isOpen and: [anObject isOpen])
         ifTrue: [handle = anObject handle]

 With no such variable that is a compile-time unknown, so the ivar is declared
 here rather than in `st/mvp_compat` — this layer loads BEFORE `st/mvp`, and a
 superclass has to exist in its final shape before the subclass that inherits
 from it is created. Declared afterwards it would have been a fresh class that
 `ResourceLibrary` was not descended from.

 REDECLARING RATHER THAN REOPENING is deliberate and safe here, and the two
 conditions that make it safe are both checked: a declaration carrying ivars
 REPLACES the class (see CLAUDE.md rule 3), and `ResourceLibrary` is the only
 subclass in the tree while `DllRegisterServer` — the one generated method
 lost — has no sender. `default` is re-supplied because the library idiom
 depends on it."
Object subclass: DynamicLinkLibrary [
    | handle |

    DynamicLinkLibrary class >> default [ ^self ]

    "Dolphin's own: `handle := nil. self handle: (self class load: aString
     flags: self loadFlags)`. Split the same way so a subclass can override
     either half."
    basicOpen: aString [
        handle := nil.
        self handle: (self class load: aString flags: self loadFlags).
        ^self
    ]
    DynamicLinkLibrary class >> load: aString flags: anInteger [
        | name h |
        name := Utf16Buffer fromString: aString.
        h := [ Kernel32 loadLibraryEx: name hFile: 0 dwFlags: anInteger ]
                ensure: [ name free ].
        (h isNil or: [ h = 0 ]) ifTrue: [ ^Win32Error signalLastError ].
        ^h
    ]
    handle [ ^handle ]
    handle: anObject [ handle := anObject ]
    isOpen [ ^handle notNil and: [ handle ~= 0 ] ]
    asParameter [ ^handle ]
    loadFlags [ ^0 ]
    close [
        handle isNil ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        Kernel32 freeLibrary: handle.
        handle := nil
    ]
    free [ ^self close ]
    beFinalizable [ ^self ]
]
